{
 "schema": "parallax-watch/1",
 "how": "Per flag, a headline scores 2 for each strong word and 1 for each weak word; the flag is set at 2 or more (one strong word, or two weak ones). Japanese words match as substrings after NFKC; ASCII words match on word boundaries, case-insensitively, plural s/es included. A word inside a longer matched word is not counted twice. `mask` words are blanked before matching. `exclude` words (sport, entertainment, weather) clear a flag, except that a strong word of money/law/security and a strong pattern of disaster (seismic intensity, magnitude, special warnings) survive. The matched words are returned with the flag, so the page can show why a story is in PRIORITY.",
 "caveat": "The words were written after looking at a small set of known cases, so the rates measured on that set are optimistic.",
 "threshold": 2,
